===== ISSUE 5 =====
title:	Add LangSmith for tracing and evals
state:	OPEN
author:	alex-moon
labels:	enhancement
comments:	0
assignees:	
projects:	
milestone:	
number:	5
--
No observability today: model calls, routing decisions and prompt assembly are one-off console.error breadcrumbs. Wire LangSmith tracing/evals around the Groq pipeline.

Suggested approach:
- Add `langsmith` npm module; env-gated (`LANGCHAIN_API_KEY`, `LANGCHAIN_PROJECT`, disable locally when unset).
- Wrap the pipeline spans: router/classifier decision (`routeQuery` in `routerService.ts`), final chat completion, and the title-generation call in `titleService.ts` — one root run per request with sessionId/userId metadata (careful: no PII/user content in run metadata; content stays in trace payloads consistent with retention settings).
- Capture token usage + latency per span from Groq usage fields, and surface `model`/`reason` from RoutingResult in run tags to correlate routing regressions.
- Evals: seed a small golden prompt set (simple vs code vs complex) and run through the router offline; assert expected model tier and answer-quality rubric via LangSmith evals, wire into CI as an optional job.
- Streaming: log aggregate output once on `done` rather than per-delta noise; record error finish on the SSE `error` path.
- Acceptance: dev session appears in LangSmith with sane spans; failing eval set demonstrates the failure before merging router changes.
===== ISSUE 4 =====
title:	More models + query enhancement/splitting/agentic behaviour
state:	OPEN
author:	alex-moon
labels:	enhancement
comments:	1
assignees:	
projects:	
milestone:	
number:	4
--
Today every turn goes through `routerService.routeQuery` → exactly one Groq model (small/large/guard), single completion, single turn.

Suggestions to evolve beyond one-prompt-one-response:
- Configurable model catalog: move model definitions out of `ROUTER_SMALL/LARGE/GUARD_MODEL` envs into a selectable catalog (e.g. llama/gpt-oss/kimi variants) so users can pick a model per chat or the router picks from a wider pool.
- Query enhancement: pre-analysis pass that expands vague prompts with clarified intent/requirements before the main model answers (cheap small-model pass, cached).
- Query decomposition/splitting: detect multi-part prompts ("...and also..."), split into sub-queries, run each with the right model, then synthesise a final answer.
- Tool/agentic loop: allow the model to call tools (web search, eval-run JS, saved-context retrieval) over multiple turns with a clean stop/max-iteration budget.
- Reasoning budget: route harder prompts to larger models with higher token budgets; stream ' Planning...' status via the existing SSE `event:` channel.
- Guardrails: keep the guard model as a pre-flight classifier, extend to input/output moderation decisions.
- intefacing: keep `/api/chat/stream` SSE contract stable (new event types are additive), persistence keeps one assistant message per turn.
- Acceptance: multi-part queries answered in full, model choice visible in `Message.modelName`, tests mock the new passes without breaking existing suites.
